---
import Document from '../../layouts/document.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import editorPackage from '../../../../editor/package.json';
import { frontmatter as indexFrontmatter } from '../../../../../docs/en/index.md';
import { useTranslations } from '../../i18n/translations.ts';
import iconMoodSad from '@tabler/icons/outline/mood-sad.svg?raw';

const t = useTranslations('en');
---

<Document title={t('index.title')}>
  <main>
    <h1 class="nl-heading nl-heading--level-1">{indexFrontmatter['title']}</h1>
    <p class="nl-paragraph">{indexFrontmatter['intro']}</p>
    <div class="utrecht-action-group">
      <a
        class="nl-button nl-button--primary"
        href="https://github.com/nl-design-system/editor"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        <span class="nl-button__label">{t('index.cta.github')}</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="nl-button nl-button--secondary"
        href="https://github.com/orgs/nl-design-system/projects/70/views/27"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        <span class="nl-button__label">{t('index.cta.roadmap')}</span>
      </a>
      <a class="nl-button nl-button--primary" href={`https://www.npmjs.com/package/${editorPackage.name}`}>
        <span class="nl-button__label">npm v{editorPackage.version}</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <Section>
      <h2 class="nl-heading nl-heading--level-2">What is Clippy?</h2>
      <p class="nl-paragraph">
        Clippy is an accessible rich-text editor for Dutch government websites. It is built on Tiptap and ships as Web
        Components, so you can use it in any framework and any CMS. Its styling comes from NL Design System design
        tokens, so content in the editor looks the same as on your website.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section>
      <h2 class="nl-heading nl-heading--level-2">What problem does Clippy solve?</h2>
      <p class="nl-paragraph">
        Many accessibility problems are introduced while writing: a skipped heading level, an image without alt text, a
        link that says "click here" or empty paragraphs used for spacing. An automated test only finds these issues once
        the page is already online.
      </p>
      <p class="nl-paragraph">
        Clippy points these problems out to editors while they write. For every notification, the editor explains what
        is wrong and how to fix it. This helps you meet WCAG 2.2 level AA and ATAG 2.0.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section>
      <h2 class="nl-heading nl-heading--level-2">How it works</h2>
      <p class="nl-paragraph">
        In this example, heading level 3 follows heading level 1 directly. Clippy marks the heading in the gutter and
        explains the issue below the text.
      </p>
      <clippy-context id="clippy-example-heading-level">
        <div slot="value">
          <h1>Heading level 1</h1>
          <h3>Heading level 3</h3>
          <p>Skipping a level is not allowed!</p>
        </div>
        <div class="clippy-guideline clippy-guideline--negative">
          <div class="clippy-guideline__description">
            <h3 class="clippy-guideline__badge clippy-guideline__badge--negative">
              <Fragment set:html={iconMoodSad} />
              <span class="clippy-guideline__title">Don't: skip heading levels</span>
            </h3>
            <p>
              Here heading level 3 follows heading level 1, so level 2 is missing. Screen reader users navigate by
              headings and then miss a level in the structure. Use heading level 2 after heading level 1.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="clippy-guideline__example">
            <div class="clippy-canvas">
              <div class="clippy-canvas__example">
                <clippy-content>
                  <clippy-validations-gutter mode="list"></clippy-validations-gutter>
                </clippy-content>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="clippy-guideline__validations">
            <clippy-validations-list></clippy-validations-list>
          </div>
        </div>
      </clippy-context>
      <p class="nl-paragraph">
        You can find more examples in the <a class="nl-link" href={t('nav.href.guidelines')}>accessibility guidelines</a
        >.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section>
      <h2 class="nl-heading nl-heading--level-2">Using Clippy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Try the full editor in the <a class="nl-link" href={t('nav.href.demo')}>demo</a>.</li>
        <li>
          Add Clippy to CKEditor 5, Drupal or TYPO3 with the <a class="nl-link" href={t('nav.href.integrations')}
            >integrations</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use the editor in a React application with the <a class="nl-link" href={t('nav.href.react')}>React wrappers</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>Configure the toolbar in the <a class="nl-link" href={t('nav.href.configuration')}>configuration</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </Section>
  </main>
</Document>
